<section class="blk blk--first">
  <p class="eyebrow">The Roadmap</p>
  <h1 class="sec">The Roadmap.</h1>
  <p class="lead">The road ahead, one milestone at a time.</p>
  <p>Dates are targets. Evidence sets the pace. The order of the stages, and the gates that protect each one — funding, safety review, legal capacity, and local operators — do not move. The calendar does, as capacity and evidence change. Day 1 is 15 July 2026.</p>
</section>

<section class="blk blk--cream2">
  <p class="eyebrow">Year one</p>
  <h2 class="sec">The first year, as directions — not promises.</h2>

  <h3>First 90 days</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>Public launch of the movement, the site, and the source library.</li>
    <li>The fiscal-sponsor application and due diligence begin.</li>
    <li>The pledge and email capture open; the first receipts-complete cost visual is published.</li>
    <li>Core policies released as public review drafts.</li>
  </ul>
  {#- SPONSOR-GATED: donations open only when a fiscal sponsor is confirmed; the deductibility line below changes at that gate. See records/SPONSOR_TRANSITION.md. -#}
  <p>Tax-deductible donations open <strong>only</strong> after sponsorship is confirmed.</p>

  <h3>Months 4–6</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>First Human Essentials Dashboard prototype.</li>
    <li>Regional methodology published.</li>
    <li>The first Shelter, Food, and Energy dossiers go deep.</li>
  </ul>

  <h3>Months 7–9</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>Project briefs and first creator partnerships.</li>
    <li>The first community survey through the advisory Assembly.</li>
    <li>Early Treasury updates, once funds move.</li>
  </ul>

  <h3>Months 10–12</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>A public progress report and partner outreach.</li>
    <li>Funding applications and a Year 2 plan.</li>
  </ul>
</section>

<section class="blk">
  <p class="eyebrow">Longer horizon</p>
  <h2 class="sec">The longer horizon.</h2>

  <h3>Year 2</h3>
  <p>More regions and sectors, a wider contributor network, and grant applications — plus the Community Resource Simulator and the Library of Things Kit moving from brief toward build.</p>

  <h3>Year 3</h3>
  <p>Partner-led, low-risk physical prototypes — but only where funding, safety review, legal capacity, and local operators already exist. Uncost publishes and supports; local operators decide and act.</p>

  <h3>Beyond</h3>
  <p>Larger integrated demonstrations, only once evidence, partners, governance, and safety capacity are mature.</p>
</section>

<section class="blk blk--cream2">
  <p class="eyebrow">How to read these dates</p>
  <h2 class="sec">How to read these dates.</h2>
  <p>Every date on this page is a movable target anchored to Day 1 (15 July 2026), not a promise. Targets shift as evidence and capacity change; the order of the stages and the gates that protect each one do not. Evidence, legal review, safety, sponsor requirements, and founder approval outrank the calendar.</p>
</section>

